 {"id":"fabro-c419","title":"Wire the planner's fabro_runs_list binding — the in-flight-PR guard silently fails open","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T19:52:43.290Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T21:16:54.036Z","description":"Node `planner` in `.fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro` declares `fabro_tools=\"fabro_runs_list\"` but the tool never reaches the agent: make the engine honor the node-level `fabro_tools` attribute (or set run-level `agent.fabro_tools` for develop), and until then reword planner.md step 4 to instruct journaling the degraded mode and proceeding when the tool is absent from the toolset, instead of implying the call is always possible. Evidence: this run's events seq 27 show `agent.tools.available` for planner@1 lists no fabro_runs_list and run settings show `agent.fabro_tools=false`; the planner's only journaled painpoint was that the in-flight-PR check degraded to a no-op — the exact failure closed fabro-06e0 and fabro-d0c7 were meant to prevent (fabro-22e4 double-pick while a PR waits in gate). Expected effect: the loop's only double-work guard actually functions, preventing a duplicated run (~$0.15 plus ~12 min each) next time a seed's PR sits in gate. ADR-0019: this finding changes a tool allowlist in an agent-reachable surface, so it is capability-affecting — implementation awaits explicit user approval. Fix direction is engine-mediated and read-only (the engine exposes its existing `fabro_runs_list` read tool via the node-level attribute); no raw clients or tokens proposed. Note: the run-level-warning sub-item duplicates open fabro-5b0a and is deliberately excluded. Basis: run 01M2183254XQ3HJ45SR4P1Y2X6, workflow version 84429d0a3253eaa52e2406a04a3b97b4365d0ff68b0cdc2f46c296e8c05ec7a6, commit 0dc16012c16ee2f6b2e61ecc73afcf0bd5f26b3d\n\nUSER DECISION (2026-09-08 evening, chat session on this machine): OPTION A APPROVED - the engine honors the node-level fabro_tools attribute (per-stage tool declaration in the workflow graph), mirroring how inspects already works per node. Scope of the approval: the graph attribute fabro_tools=\"fabro_runs_list\" on the develop planner node surfaces the READ-ONLY, engine-mediated fabro_runs_list tool in that stage's agent session; least privilege per stage (ADR-0019.2/.3 - extend existing tools, no credentials, no raw clients). No other tool, stage, or workflow is covered by this approval. The interim prompt line (planner.md step 4: journal the degraded mode when the tool is absent) stays part of this seed's implementation. fe15 (toolchain image bake) is NOT covered - separate needs-user decision, still open.","labels":["revision","engine","workflows"],"assignee":"fabro","closedAt":"2026-09-08T21:16:54.036Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-fe15","title":"Bake a debug fabro-cli (or shared cargo cache) into the run toolchain image","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T19:52:50.145Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T19:52:50.145Z","description":"In the `fabro-toolchain:noble` Dockerfile used for develop run containers (`.fabro/Dockerfile*`), pre-build `fabro-cli` in debug profile or mount a shared cargo cache across run containers so `target/debug/fabro` exists at container start. Evidence: this run's implementer probed `ls target/debug/fabro` and found nothing (seq 107) — the container starts with an empty `target/`, so any run legitimately needing the CLI pays ~7 min of cold build; the workflow graph comment already measures a cold gate at ~15 min worst case. Expected effect: the first cargo invocation in every run drops from minutes to seconds, independent of prompt compliance; complements the config-only smoke cost-tiering for seeds that still need built checks. Distinct from open fabro-cfd6 (prebuilt cargo-chef image for the CI gate, not run containers) and closed fabro-513e (human-facing just recipe). ADR-0019: this finding adds a binary to the agent-reachable toolchain image surface, so it is capability-affecting — implementation awaits explicit user approval. Fix direction stays engine-mediated (image build content / engine-managed cache mount; the prebuilt binary is the repo's own read-write CLI, no new credentials or external clients). Basis: run 01M2183254XQ3HJ45SR4P1Y2X6, workflow version 84429d0a3253eaa52e2406a04a3b97b4365d0ff68b0cdc2f46c296e8c05ec7a6, commit 0dc16012c16ee2f6b2e61ecc73afcf0bd5f26b3d","labels":["needs-user","revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-e33d","title":"Add closest-match hint to edit_file errors and pin old_string sourcing in implementer prompt","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T20:11:15.657Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T09:40:29.001Z","description":"In run 01M219SFJ6A75DS2BP77TBENQZ (seq 92-97) the implementer's first edit_file failed with a bare 'old_string not found in file' because it rebuilt old_string from read_file's line-numbered rendering (reconstructed 4-space indent vs the file's 3-space), burned a cat -A diagnostic round, and journaled a wrong 'transient matcher hiccup' lesson durably. Change: (a) at lib/components/fabro-agent/src/tools.rs:234 include the line number of the closest fuzzy match / first diverging whitespace in the error; (b) add one line to .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md: build old_string from raw sed -n output, never from the line-numbered read_file rendering. Complementary to fabro-645d (scoped reads via sed -n), not superseding it. Effect: removes one diagnostic plus one LLM round per mismatch and prevents false 'transient' conclusions from being recorded as lore. Basis: run 01M219SFJ6A75DS2BP77TBENQZ, workflow version 84429d0a3253eaa52e2406a04a3b97b4365d0ff68b0cdc2f46c296e8c05ec7a6, commit aed06d18be94f10f758651dcaf0eadb97f5d0c17","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
-{"id":"fabro-8bf4","title":"Engine: lint stage completion when a key declared in context_allow_keys was never emitted","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T21:24:48.800Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T10:31:39.470Z","description":"Run 01M21BG1TG9SNM4QAS2A33W6GF (seed fabro-c419, PR #76): develop planner@1 emitted context_updates with no journal key at all despite the node declaring context_allow_keys=...,journal and the prompt calling silence a violation; that same pass ran the in-flight-PR guard degraded to a no-op and nothing recorded either miss. Add a completion lint to the stage-envelope validation in lib/components/fabro-workflow (alongside the fabro-900e/e47c producer lints): a stage completing without emitting any key declared in its context_allow_keys emits a visible warning or consumes one output_retries nudge. Scoped as the general allow-keys visibility lint; journal-specific output-schema enforcement is already tracked by fabro-017f (cross-ref, not superseded). Expected effect: missing journal reports and fail-open guards become auditable instead of silently lost. Basis: run 01M21BG1TG9SNM4QAS2A33W6GF, workflow version 84429d0a3253eaa52e2406a04a3b97b4365d0ff68b0cdc2f46c296e8c05ec7a6, commit eed7be36252face1b5316bcd9264627fb3da7fde","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
