 {"id":"fabro-9fa2","title":"Develop planner prompt: stale-basis fast path when the seed pins line anchors in its USER DECISION","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T21:24:53.260Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T09:40:28.922Z","description":"planner@1 in run 01M21BG1TG9SNM4QAS2A33W6GF spent ~13 sequential read probes and 98.3s inference / $0.123 re-deriving exact line numbers (api.rs:1345-1357, server.rs:4514) the seed's USER DECISION note already pinned, and its reasoning trace nearly misjudged the seed as already-implemented ('Stale basis?'). In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 3, add: when the seed body carries a line-pinned USER DECISION or verified basis, one spot-check grep suffices instead of full re-derivation. Complementary to fabro-645d (implementer-side scoped reads; cross-ref, not superseded). Expected effect: planner drops from ~13 calls/98s toward ~5 calls/40s (~$0.05 + ~1 min per run) and lowers the risk of wrongly closing a valid seed as superseded. Basis: run 01M21BG1TG9SNM4QAS2A33W6GF, workflow version 84429d0a3253eaa52e2406a04a3b97b4365d0ff68b0cdc2f46c296e8c05ec7a6, commit eed7be36252face1b5316bcd9264627fb3da7fde","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-1409","title":"PR postlude: append per-stage cost/time table and journal painpoint digest to the PR body","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T21:25:00.145Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T09:40:28.847Z","description":"In run 01M21BG1TG9SNM4QAS2A33W6GF, 82% of spend ($0.775) and 60% of wall sat in the implementer stage, visible only in the run conclusion, not on PR #76 that the user merges. Where the engine composes the PR postlude (same area open seed fabro-6a5a targets for auto-merge/PR-body model-call fixes; cross-ref, not superseded), append the per-stage timing/cost table plus a digest of journal painpoints. Degraded-guard notices in the PR body are intentionally excluded — already tracked by fabro-5b0a. Expected effect: at merge time the user sees that builds dominate (the case for toolchain warming, fabro-fe15) without opening the run dashboard. Basis: run 01M21BG1TG9SNM4QAS2A33W6GF, workflow version 84429d0a3253eaa52e2406a04a3b97b4365d0ff68b0cdc2f46c296e8c05ec7a6, commit eed7be36252face1b5316bcd9264627fb3da7fde","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-a18d","title":"Planner: observations naming consistency work must become current_seed_brief bullets","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T09:12:29.966Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T10:03:46.161Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md steps 6/7, require that any journal observation naming required consistency or scope work be folded into current_seed_brief as an explicit bullet (or explicitly waived there). Basis: run 01M22PCGN4E3X1XGN630MDDH39 — the planner journaled 'the same rule is referenced again at line 78 … which the implementer should keep consistent' but added no brief bullet, so the implementer kept the mechanical-rewrite paragraph verbatim, leaving prompt text ('verify with ONE focused check') contradictory with the new tests-touched rule this seed introduced; the latent inconsistency shipped through an approving review because the reviewer checks bullets, not journals. Effect: prevents self-contradictory prompt text surviving the loop; zero-cost correctness win. Basis: run 01M22PCGN4E3X1XGN630MDDH39, workflow version e6202c3d2f79d43966a4f1fc60620f8b3f3d8c36f6facf82a41cd18b0c9c1b4e, commit 6d05194d18b7f1085cbac66a27b5cee0defacce9","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro","closedAt":"2026-09-09T10:03:46.161Z"}
